  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Drought Response and Recovery in Somali Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somali Region, Ethiopia</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The package of activities for emergency response will target communities and health centres with high numbers of malnourished children under 5 and will include cash, hygiene promotion, distribution of key hygiene promotion items, nutrition and sanitation training and repair water points. Recovery activities will focus on longer term initiatives focusing on environmental degradation and climate change adaption with water spreading weirs and livelihood activities building on previous interventions of NLRC with the potential to scale up in other areas under future resilience projects.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will build on previous NLRC projects but will specifically target drought affected communities not only on emergency response but also focusing on longer-term recovery activities for targeted communities. The one-year time frame for the project supports this approach.</narrative>
  </description>
